<title>CANADA: Shell Canada raises posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Shell Canada raises posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Canada Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$11.00/cubic metre or C$1.75/barrel, to C$210.00/cubic metre or C$33.39/barrel effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$204.00/cubic metre, or C$32.43/barrel</p>
<p>Hardisty medium C$189.00/cubic metre, or C$30.05/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$177.00/cubic metre, or C$28.14/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
